.send_mtu as u64 * 1_000_000 / self.max_bw\n320\t        } else {\n321\t            margin\n322\t        };\n323\t        self.min_rtt_margin = margin;\n324\t    }\n325\t\n326\t    /// C: `BBRAdvanceLatestDeliverySignals` (picoquic/bbr.c:1007)\n327\t    ///\n328\t    /// Called near the end of ACK processing: if this ACK completed a\n329\t    /// loss round, reset `bw_latest` and `inflight_latest` to the\n330\t    /// current sample so the next round starts fresh.\n331\t    pub fn advance_latest_delivery_signals(&mut self, rs: &BbrPerAckState) {\n332\t        if self.loss_round_start {\n333\t            self.bw_latest = rs.delivery_rate;\n334\t            self.inflight_latest = rs.delivered;\n335\t        }\n336\t    }\n337\t\n338\t    /// C: `BBRBDPMultipleWithBw` (picoquic/bbr.c:869)\n339\t    ///\n340\t    /// Returns `gain × BDP` computed at the supplied `bw` rather than\n341\t    /// `self.bw`.  When `min_rtt` has never been measured (`u64::MAX`),\n342\t    /// returns the initial congestion window as a safe floor.\n343\t    ///\n344\t    /// Side-effect: writes `self.bdp` so callers can read the raw BDP\n345\t    /// estimate after the call (mirrors C's write-through of\n346\t    /// `bbr_state->bdp`).\n347\t    pub fn bdp_multiple_with_bw(&mut self, path_x: &Path, gain: f64, bw: u64) -> u64 {\n348\t        if self.min_rtt == u64::MAX {\n349\t            return CWIN_INITIAL * path_x.send_mtu as u64;\n350\t        }\n351\t        // PICOQUIC_BYTES_FROM_RATE(min_rtt_us, bps) = min_rtt * bps / 1_000_000\n352\t        self.bdp = self.min_rtt * bw / 1_000_000;\n353\t        (gain * self.bdp as f64) as u64\n354\t    }\n355\t\n356\t    /// C: `BBRBoundBWForModel` (picoquic/bbr.c:1094)\n357\t    ///\n358\t    /// Set `self.bw = min(max_bw, bw_lo, bw_hi)`.  `bw_hi` is only\n359\t    /// applied when non-zero; the zero check preserves compatibility\n360\t    /// with states where `bw_hi` is not yet initialised (noted as a\n361\t    /// TODO in the C source).\n362\t    p