UNDS_THRESHOLD;\n441\t                self.app_limited_round_count = 0;\n442\t            }\n443\t            self.app_limited_this_round = 0;\n444\t        } else {\n445\t            self.app_limited_this_round |= rs.is_app_limited as i32;\n446\t        }\n447\t        app_limited_ended\n448\t    }\n449\t\n450\t    /// C: `BBRExitLostFeedback` (picoquic/bbr.c:782)\n451\t    ///\n452\t    /// Restore the congestion window saved by `BBREnterLostFeedback` and\n453\t    /// clear the lost-feedback flag.  No-op if the flag is not set.\n454\t    pub fn exit_lost_feedback(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path) {\n455\t        if self.is_handling_lost_feedback {\n456\t            path_x.cwin = self.cwin_before_lost_feedback;\n457\t            self.is_handling_lost_feedback = false;\n458\t        }\n459\t    }\n460\t\n461\t    /// C: `BBRHasElapsedInPhase` (picoquic/bbr.c:1776)\n462\t    ///\n463\t    /// Returns `true` when `current_time` has advanced past\n464\t    /// `cycle_stamp + interval`.  Used to decide when to transition from\n465\t    /// DOWN/CRUISE to REFILL in the probe-BW cycle.\n466\t    pub(crate) fn has_elapsed_in_phase(&self, interval: u64, current_time: u64) -> bool {\n467\t        current_time > self.cycle_stamp + interval\n468\t    }\n469\t\n470\t    /// C: `BBREnterStartupResume` (picoquic/bbr.c:1972)\n471\t    ///\n472\t    /// Enter `StartupResume` state, which uses Hystart-like pacing gains\n473\t    /// to resume quickly after a suspension.  Called either when a BDP\n474\t    /// seed is set or on the initial `EnterStartup` path when a seed\n475\t    /// exists.\n476\t    pub(crate) fn enter_startup_resume(&mut self) {\n477\t        self.state = BbrAlgState::StartupResume;\n478\t        self.pacing_gain = BBR_STARTUP_RESUME_PACING_GAIN;\n479\t        self.cwnd_gain = BBR_STARTUP_RESUME_CWND_GAIN;\n480\t    }\n481\t\n482\t    /// C: `BBREnterStartup` (picoquic/bbr.c:2061)\n483\t    ///\n484\t    /// Enter normal `Startup` state with the standard pacing and cwnd\n485\t    /// gains.  Sets `is_cca_probing_up` to inform the transport that the\n486\t    /// congestion controller is actively probing for more bandwidth.\n487\t    pub fn enter_startup(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path) {\n488\t        self.state = BbrAlgState::Startup;\n489\t        self.pacing_gain = BBR_STARTUP_PACING_GAIN;\n490\t        self.cwnd_gain = BBR_STARTUP_CWND_GAIN;\n491\t        path_x.is_cca_probing_up = true;\n492\t    }\n493\t\n494\t    /// C: `BBREnterStartupLongRTT` (picoquic/bbr.c:2080)\n495\t    ///\n496\t    /// Enter `StartupLongRTT` state, which uses Hystart rather than the\n497\t    /// normal BBR Startup algorithm.  The initial congestion window is\n498\t    /// scaled up from `CWIN_INITIAL` proportional to `rtt_min` (capped at\n499\t    /// the satellite-RTT ceiling) and then further boosted by the BDP seed\n500\t    /// when available.\n501\t    pub fn enter_startup_long_rtt(&mut self, path_x: &mut Path) {\n502\t        let mut cwnd = CWIN_INITIAL;\n503\t        self.state = BbrAlgState::StartupLongRtt;\n504\t        if path_x.rtt_min > TARGET_RENO_RTT {\n505\t            let rtt_cap = if path_x.rtt_min > TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT {\n506\t                TARGET_SATELLITE_RTT\n507\t            } else {\n508\t                path_x.rtt_min\n509\t            };\n510\t            cwnd = (cwnd as f64 * rtt_cap.ticks() as f64 / TARGET_RENO_RTT.ticks() as f64) as u64;\n511\t        }\n512\t        if cwnd < self.bdp_seed {\n513\t            cwnd = self.bdp_seed;\n514\t        }\n515\t        if cwnd > path_x.cwin {\n516\t            path_x.cwin = cwnd;\n517\t        }\n518\t        path_x.is_cca_probing_up = true;\n519\t    }\n520\t\n521\t    /// C: `BBRInitFullPipe` (picoquic/bbr.c:434)\n522\t    ///\n523\t    /// Reset the \"pipe full\" bandwidth-growth detector to its initial state.\n524\t    pub fn init_full_pipe(&mut self) {\n525\t        self.filled_pipe = false;\n526\t        self.full_bw = 0;\n527\t        self.full_bw_count = 0;\n528\t    }\n529\t\n530\t    /// C: `BBRInitLowerBounds` (picoquic/bbr.c:1025)\n531\t    ///\n532\t    /// On the first congestion episode in a cycle, latch `bw_lo` to\n533\t    /// `max_bw` and `inflight_lo` to `cwin` (the UINT64_MAX sentinel\n534\t    /// means \"not yet initialised\").\n535\t    pub fn init_lower_bounds(&mut self, path_x: &Path) {\n536\t        if self.bw_lo == u64::MAX {\n537\t            self.bw_lo = self.max_bw;\n538\t        }\n539\t        if self.inflight_lo == u64::MAX {\n540\t            self.inflight_lo = path_x.cwin;\n541\t        }\n542\t    }\n543\t\n544\t    /// C: `BBRInitPacingRate` (picoquic/bbr.c:933)\n545\t    ///\n546\t    /// Set the initial pacing rate based on the nominal bandwidth at\n547\t    /// `INITIAL_RTT` (250 ms), unless the path already has a real RTT\n548\t    /// estimate, in which case that estimate is used instead.\n549\t    pub fn init_pacing_rate(&mut self, path_x: &Path) {\n550\t        let initial_rtt = if path_x.smoothed_rtt != INITIAL_RTT || path_x.rtt_variant.ticks() != 0 {\n551\t            path_x.smoothed_rtt.ticks()\n552\t        } else {\n553\t            INITIAL_RTT.ticks()\n554\t        };\n555\t        let nominal_bandwidth = (1_000_000u64 * CWIN_INITIAL) as f64 / initial_rtt as f64;\n556\t        self.pacing_rate = BBR_STARTUP_PACING_GAIN * nominal_bandwidth;\n557\t    }\n558\t\n559\t    /// C: `BBRInitRandom` (picoquic/bbr.c:421)\n560\t    ///\n561\t    /// Seed `random_context` from the current time, connection role, and\n562\t    /// path ID so that tests remain deterministic while production runs\n563\t    /// diverge.  `connection` is passed separately because `Path` carries\n564\t    /// no back-pointer to its owning `Connection` in Rust.\n565\t    pub fn init_random(&mut self, connection: &Connection, path_x: &Path, current_time: u64) {\n566\t        let mut ctx: u64 = 0xfedcba9876543210;\n567\t        ctx ^= current_time;\n568\t        if connection.client_mode {\n569\t            ctx = ctx.wrapping_add(0x0123456789abcdef);\n570\t        }\n571\t        if path_x.unique_path_id > 0 && path_x.unique_path_id != u64::MAX {\n572\t            ctx = ctx.wrapping_mul(path_x.unique_path_id.wrapping_add(1));\n573\t        }\n574\t        self.random_context = ctx;\n575\t    }\n576\t\n577\t    /// C: `BBRInflightWithHeadroom` (picoquic/bbr.c:1547)\n578\t    ///\n579\t    /// Returns the inflight limit that leaves `BBRHeadroom` (15%) of the\n580\t    /// bottleneck buffer free for competing flows.  Returns `u64::MAX`\n581\t    /// when `inflight_hi` has not yet been measured.\n582\t    pub fn inflight_with_headroom(&self, path_x: &Path) -> u64 {\n583\t        const BBR_HEADROOM: f64 = 0.15;\n584\t        const BBR_MIN_PIPE_CWND: u64 = 4;\n585\t        if self.inflight_hi == u64::MAX {\n586\t            return u64::MAX;\n587\t        }\n588\t        let headroom = ((1.0 - BBR_HEADROOM) * self.inflight_hi as f64) as u64;\n589\t        headroom.max(BBR_MIN_PIPE_CWND * path_x.send_mtu as u64)\n590\t    }\n591\t\n592\t    /// C: `BBRIsProbingBW` (picoquic/bbr.c:1532)\n593\t    ///\n594\t    /// Returns `true` when the state is actively probing for more bandwidth\n595\t    /// (i.e. NOT in one of the non-probing states: ProbeBwDown, ProbeBwCruise,\n596\t    /// Drain, or ProbeRtt).\n597\t    pub fn is_probing_bw(&self) -> bool {\n598\t        !matches!(\n599\t            self.state,\n600\t            BbrAlgState::ProbeBwDown\n601\t                | BbrAlgState::ProbeBwCruise\n602\t                | BbrAlgState::Drain\n603\t                | BbrAlgState::ProbeRtt\n604\t        )\n605\t    }\n606\t\n607\t    /// C: `BBRLossLowerBounds` (picoquic/bbr.c:1035)\n608\t    ///\n609\t    /// Apply a `BBRBeta` (0.7) multiplicative decrease to `bw_lo` and\n610\t    /// `inflight_lo`, then floor each at the latest sample so the model\n611\t    /// cannot shrink below what was actually observed this round.\n612\t    pub fn loss_lower_bounds(&mut self) {\n613\t        self.bw_lo = ((BBR_BETA * self.bw_lo as f64) as u64).max(self.bw_latest);\n614\t        self.inflight_lo = ((BBR_BETA * self.inflight_lo as f64) as u64).max(self.inflight_latest);\n615\t    }\n616\t\n617\t    /// C: `BBRModulateCwndForRecovery` (picoquic/bbr.c:627)\n618\t    ///\n619\t    /// On packet loss, shrink `cwin` by the number of bytes lost (floored at\n620\t    /// one MTU).  When `packet_conservation` is active, ensure `cwin` is at\n621\t    /// least `bytes_in_transit + newly_acked` so the pipe stays full.\n622\t    pub fn modulate_cwnd_for_recovery(&self, path_x: &mut Path, rs: &BbrPerAckState) {\n623\t        if rs.newly_lost > 0 {\n624\t            if path_x.cwin > rs.newly_lost + path_x.send_mtu as u64 {\n625\t                path_x.cwin -= rs.newly_lost;\n626\t            } else {\n627\t                path_x.cwin = path_x.send_mtu as u64;\n628\t            }\n629\t        }\n630\t        if self.packet_conservation && path_x.cwin < path_x.bytes_in_transit + rs.newly_acked {\n631\t            path_x.cwin = path_x.bytes_in_transit + rs.newly_acked;\n632\t        }\n633\t    }\n634\t\n635\t    /// C: `BBRRaiseInflightHiSlope` (picoquic/bbr.c:1561)\n636\t    ///\n637\t    /// Recompute how aggressively `inflight_hi` is raised during ProbeBwUp.\n638\t    /// Each round the slope doubles (shift by `bw_probe_up_rounds`, capped at\n639\t    /// 30), and `bw_probe_up_cnt` is set to the number of MTU-sized ACKs\n640\t    /// required to justify a one-MTU increase (minimum 1).\n641\t    pub fn raise_inflight_hi_slope(&mut self, path_x: &Path) {\n642\t        let growth_this_round = (path_x.send_mtu as u64) << self.bw_probe_up_rounds;\n643\t        self.bw_probe_up_rounds = (self.bw_probe_up_rounds + 1).min(30);\n644\t        let up_cnt = (path_x.cwin / growth_this_round) as u32;\n645\t        self.bw_probe_up_cnt = up_cnt.max(1);\n646\t    }\n647\t\n648\t    /// C: `BBRResetCongestionSignals` (picoquic/bbr.c:1014)\n649\t    ///\n650\t    /// Clear the per-round congestion signals